cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this software when using the ESAW-Link implementations or reproduction tools. Paper metadata will be added when the manuscript is published."
type: software
title: "ESAW-Link: Reproducibility Sources"
authors:
  - family-names: Messina
    given-names: Valerio
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-19
license: MIT
abstract: "Source code, ESAW adaptations of hierarchical text classification baselines, configurations and verification tools accompanying the ESAW-Link study. Institutional data, private split identifiers, per-record predictions and model checkpoints are excluded. Incomplete experimental gates are documented explicitly."
keywords:
  - ESAW
  - occupational accident coding
  - dense retrieval
  - hierarchical text classification
  - reproducibility
